# Snocone (scrip-snocone), program 1: numbers and factorials. developer_03 2026-11-22. Cells counted from 0 among the CODE cells (the cao's rule), lines from 1 in the cell. Written from the step law of skill debugger section 2 BEFORE any run: a step in at a call enters the function; a step out and a next that leave a routine stop at the first stop in a shallower frame; a next at a line that calls a routine steps over the call; a value is in the language's image (an integer 2, a string 'x'); a frame at a call is at the line of its call.
# REWRITTEN from the step law (skill debugger 2a) by the cfo 2026-11-25 after cause P (the head of a while stops at every test): a breakpoint inside a call stops a next first, so every Fact(n) of the recursion is a stop of the breakpoint at line 16; the head of the run cell's while is a stop at every test; each stop worked out by hand from the program before any run; read 230 of 230 TRUE on SCRIP 98967fcfd.
